## Completion evidence (2026-10-15)

Implemented structured "'`needs_input` executor results, durable question identity and
main-session publication/input requests through the existing OpenCode adapter. Questions
carry requirement, recommendation, run, issue, job, operation, attempt, epoch and artifact
revisions. Only the affected issue and descendants wait; the executor releases its slot
and owned environment before human waiting. Unsupported human-input capability remains
visible on the pending question instead of consuming an attempt.

A correlated clarification continues the same worktree, base commit and attempt with a
fresh job ID, current approved PRD/issue context and retained question history. Human
waiting has no timer; the remaining active executor deadline survives continuation.
Answers from unrelated sessions, old/superseded requests or artifact revisions, stale
attempts/control epochs and duplicate messages cannot advance work. Current durable
state is re-read before every transition; old dispatch completions cannot overwrite a
new continuation.

User-correlated `revise_scope` answers supply complete proposed PRD/graph/issue content.
Content hashes determine whether artifacts actually changed; graph validation precedes
publication. Draft publication uses the existing intent/atomic-directory mechanism and
normal combined execution approval gate. Previous artifacts, approval and integrated
work evidence are retained, and affected/already-integrated IDs appear in the approval
presentation. Only renewed approval rebinds the unchanged validated baseline; affected
integrated work is scheduled against the revised artifacts with evidence retained. The
questioning issue resumes its existing attempt. Other pending questions receive fresh
revision-bound identities. Public router methods accept later host responses and continue
planning; adapter-delivered responses continue automatically. No browser mutation route,
package publication, external message or target-branch merge was introduced.

