This task was already finished by an earlier run in this iteration. I re-ran the checks, and one problem was left: the repo-wide lint failed. That is now fixed and all three validation commands pass.

**What was already in place:**
- When an executor needs input, its question is saved against the run, issue, attempt and plan version, and posted to the main OpenCode chat.
- Only that issue and the issues depending on it wait; independent issues keep running.
- Waiting for an answer doesn't run down the agent timeout and doesn't use up a retry.
- Answers from an unrelated session, for an outdated question, or sent twice are rejected.
- If the answer changes the PRD or issue graph, that work can't run under the old approval; it needs a new approval first.

**Results from this run:**
- `bun run typecheck`: passed.
- `bun test tests/integration/09-questions.test.ts`: 4 passed, 0 failed (58 assertions). This covers the demo scenario: B waits on a question while C and E finish, then B resumes after the answer without starting a new attempt.
- `bun run lint`: it failed on a formatting error in `tests/browser/dashboard.test.ts`, a test file from another slice. I ran the formatter on that one file; the change is whitespace only. Lint now passes.

I ticked the type-check-and-lint box in `.agents/issues/9-resolve-executor-questions-in-opencode.md` and added these results to its completion notes.

